# <CLIENT> — infrastructure

> Written by `create-mds` into `infra/README.md`. Describes **where** this deployment's
> infrastructure lives — **no secrets**. Credentials never live here: the SSH private key stays on
> the operator's laptop, the BigQuery service-account key stays on the VPS, and provider tokens live
> under `~/.config/agentic-data-engineer/`. How the agent drives these hosts:
> skillpack's `shared-references/remote-control-model.md`.

## VPS

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Provider | <hostinger / "reused: provider"> |
| Tailnet hostname | <vps-tailnet-host> |
| Public IP | <public-ip> — emergency only; port 22 closed to non-tailnet machines after lockdown |
| Login user | `deploy` |
| Access (default) | `ssh deploy@<vps-tailnet-host>` — Tailscale SSH, keyless |
| Access (fallback) | `ssh -i ~/.ssh/<client>_vps deploy@<vps-tailnet-host>` |
| SSH key (local) | `~/.ssh/<client>_vps` — laptop-only, gitignored, **never committed** |

